From: phlink <phlink@local>
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] phlink: hard-disable crash report uploads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GetCollectStatsConsent() now returns false at the very top, before any
BRANDING / ChromeOS / settings lookup. Crashpad still produces local
minidumps under <profile>/Crashpad/ for self-debugging, only the
uploader path is dead. Survives any future refactor of the
GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING gate. PRD §3.5, TELM-02.
---
 chrome/app/chrome_crash_reporter_client.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/app/chrome_crash_reporter_client.cc b/chrome/app/chrome_crash_reporter_client.cc
index f0c0ff0871ee9..50619620c377d 100644
--- a/chrome/app/chrome_crash_reporter_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_crash_reporter_client.cc
@@ -169,6 +169,13 @@ bool ChromeCrashReporterClient::IsRunningUnattended() {
 }
 
 bool ChromeCrashReporterClient::GetCollectStatsConsent() {
+  // phlink: never upload crash reports. Crashpad still produces local
+  // minidumps under <profile>/Crashpad/ which are useful for self-debug,
+  // but the uploader path is hard-disabled here in addition to the
+  // GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING check below (PRD §3.5, TELM-02). This survives
+  // any upstream refactor that drops the BRANDING gate.
+  return false;
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING)
   bool is_official_chrome_build = true;
 #else
